.TH PWATCH 1
.SH NAME
pwatch \\- sample Linux process state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pwatch
pwatch --pid PID [--interval DURATION] [--count NUMBER] [--format json|ndjson]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Passively samples process state, RSS, and thread count. It does not attach a debugger or send signals.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBpwatch --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
